WEBVTT

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.930
So full, so full! Bravo to you, Mariana.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.400
Please! The dishes I presented
were ones that Master Danblf liked,

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.480
so I am glad if they were
to your taste, Miss Mira.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:36.030
Because I am Danblf...
When might I possibly tell Mariana this?

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.950
Looks like a messenger on
horseback from the Royal Palace.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:18.010
Seriously, you summon
people without reserve...

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.430
Of course, there's
an important matter at hand.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.600
"Episode 3
'I'm... a Big Softie When It Comes
to These Things'"
An important matter, or so you say.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.350
Before that, shall we get you
a change of clothes?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.310
This way, please.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.400
Now, Miss Mira, arms up!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:34.480
Huh? See here now!
What are you doing?!

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.280
--You have a very shapely figure.
How adorable.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.610
--Come on! No! I said, no!
--You have a very shapely figure.
How adorable.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:39.490
--Now, please raise your foot.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.740
--What? So, that's how you wear that...
--Now, please raise your foot.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.580
--What? So, that's how you wear that...
--Oh, never mind that. I do not like this!

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.330
Is it so important that I
wear these clothes?

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:57.050
It suits you well. It's a masterpiece
of Lily's and the other maids.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:02.430
If Luminaria sees me,
she will mock me again.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:06.890
Don't worry. I had Luminaria
go protect the north.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:10.230
Even so, the clothes really do suit you.

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:11.980
No way!

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:15.610
Oh, come on. You actually
rather like it, don't you?

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.440
Now, regarding the main issue
I had you come here for today...

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.900
Seriously. Out with it already.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:24.990
Defense of the Three Great Kingdoms.
Ten years ago. Already heard of it?

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:31.500
Remember when you started the game,
you first joined one of three kingdoms?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.870
As a kind of tutorial?

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.630
Yes, we did.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:38.960
Unlike the new kingdoms we players
created, these initial three kingdoms

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.380
couldn't be destroyed
under normal circumstances.

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.800
They existed as these powerful kingdoms.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.600
However, one day, a massive horde
of demons came flying out of the sky.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.270
And the whole continent
got embroiled in a great war

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:54.060
between humans and demons.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.900
In the end, the humans managed
to annihilate the demons somehow.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.320
But after the war ended,
everyone was busy with rebuilding.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.620
It wasn't the time for humans
to be fighting each other,

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:10.660
so in order to contain one another, the
"Limited Non-Aggression Pact" was formed.

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:16.080
Simply explained, its objective
was to ban war for ten years

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:20.880
after the agreement was signed, and to
let each kingdom regain their strength.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.800
Hmm, and I presume
the pact is ending soon.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.350
Very perceptive of you.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.680
And now, this land
is in a difficult position.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:37.560
As you know, this kingdom was kept safe
by the existence of you Nine Wise Men.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.150
I want you to look at this.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:43.610
As this Friends List shows,
you were the last one.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:46.360
Yes, everyone is already online.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:50.700
If that's the case, why are they
all not here in this time of crisis?

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.830
That's what I can't figure out.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.540
But Danblf,

00:04:54.540 --> 00:05:00.380
you appeared before me in this way,
just in the nick of time.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.090
I felt that this was fate.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.720
Fate, is it?

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:09.550
The Nine Wise Men are a crafty,
intractable bunch.

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.680
So I won't insist on all of them.
Even just half is fine.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.270
We need to find enough
fighting strength to protect

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:18.520
this kingdom in the next year,
while the Pact still keeps us safe.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:20.820
Danblf, the One-Man Army...

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.230
No, Mira, the wise man's pupil,

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:29.030
I command you in the name of Solomon!
Find the Nine Wise Men of Alcait!

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:32.370
As you wish, my king.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:38.500
"{Main Quest}
Find the Nine Wise Men of Alcait"

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:43.000
However... I'm not exactly
sure where to start.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.800
How about Nebrapolis?

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.090
Soul Howl!

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.350
That's right. Soul Howl,
the Great Wall.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.390
Elder of the Tower of Necromancy

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:57.810
and a lover of immortality
to the point of obsession.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:01.980
I believe the Ancient Temple Nebrapolis,
also called the catacombs,

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:03.610
was a paradise for him.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.940
I see. Speaking of Nebrapolis,
it's the dungeon where slumbers

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:09.530
the Mirror of Darkness, which
allows you to converse with the dead.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:13.540
It certainly seems like there's a good
chance he's in those catacombs.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.910
He was such a depressing guy.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.920
Then, I'll leave it to you.

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.130
As for the adventurer's license
to enter the dungeon,

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.750
I'll make the arrangements with the Union.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.300
And I've had Garrett prepare,
so he's ready to move.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:28.930
So you're telling me
to go right this instant?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:32.050
Of course, strike while the iron's hot.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.730
Good grief. But I told Mariana
that I'd be back soon.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.270
Oh, also,

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.890
if you're going to Nebrapolis,

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:43.480
there's a little something I'd like you
to check while you're there.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:56.160
I wonder around what time
will Miss Mira return today?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.540
Garrett!

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.500
So, you've finally done it.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:09.380
P-Please wait, Miss Mira!
This person suddenly jumped out.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:12.300
Are you okay? No deep wounds...

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:17.810
What's this? Did you run over a zombie?

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.430
Zombie?!

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:23.440
They've been showing up
a lot around here recently.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.440
However, they don't attack humans,

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.860
and about the only damage
they do is to trample the fields.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.070
Zombies are nocturnal in the first place.

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:35.200
They avoid light during the day
and lurk in the forest shadows...

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.240
Hmm. It's obviously different.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:47.630
Hmm, so this is the adventurer's license.
But this case is awfully girly...

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:54.470
What's this? I'm bumping
into a lot of things today.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.430
Are you okay, boy? Are you hurt?

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.310
Oh, no. Sorry to run into you.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.810
He's there--the boy from earlier!

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:07.520
Seriously, he ran off so suddenly...

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.900
Who are you folk? Might you be kidnappers?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.320
You're wrong!
What a terrible thing to say!

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.780
Oh, an adventurer's license?

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.790
You're the same as me.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.160
Miss, you're a C-Rank adventurer?

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.370
What?! This little girl?

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.790
She's a summoner?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:30.090
If you're deceived by appearances,
you still have a long way to go.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:32.340
So, what happened with this kid?

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:36.590
Oh, um... this kid made us
a kind of crazy request.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:41.350
When we refused, he ran away crying,
so we were worried and chased him.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.140
Oh... so, what's the request?

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.150
Please! Take me to Nebrapolis!

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:51.360
See? Crazy request, right?

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:56.070
Taking a little kid like him
to that dangerous dungeon...

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.950
Tell me why.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.750
I want to see my mom and dad!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:05.210
They're both adventurers,
and I was told they're dead.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:09.840
But I heard there's a mirror in Nebrapolis
that lets you see the dead!

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.130
He means the Mirror of Darkness.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:17.140
I want to see my mom and dad!
Just one glimpse!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.060
"{Subquest}
Escort the Boy to Nebrapolis"

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.060
Is this a subquest?

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:25.520
I see, so that's what this is about.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.350
I don't mind helping.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:33.230
Coincidentally, I was planning to
drop by there, so you can come, too.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:35.030
Th-Thank you very much!

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:36.780
My name is Tact!

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:39.160
Wait a minute! Just like that?!

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.240
It's beyond reckless, going with
a little kid you have to protect!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.290
All that needs to happen is for me
to keep him safe, right?

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:49.670
What?! W-Wait! I understand!

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.380
My name is Emella. I'll go with you!

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.460
Can't be helped...

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.180
They're so late.
Both of them arriving tardy?

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.220
Hey!

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:05.180
Ah, you've brought so many with you.

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:09.440
Sorry, sorry! My guild
is called Écarlate Carillon.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:12.940
Just to be safe, I brought
some of our other members.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:18.410
Hey. So, you're Mira? I'm Asval.
Nice to meet you.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.910
I'm Flicker. Nice to meet you.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.620
I'm Mira. This is Tact.

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:27.250
This dewy freshness...

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:33.460
This is the unmistakable soft skin
of a virgin! S-Smells so good! Mira!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.920
Hey, Flicker!

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.550
I give up, I give up!

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:40.640
I'm sorry, Mira. I know
how we come across,

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:43.390
but we're technically
high-level adventurers.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:47.350
I see. You've been blessed with
some good chance encounters, Tact.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.640
Yeah.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.770
Except for some...

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.860
Well then, shall we go?

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.490
Let's confirm.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:01.450
We're headed for the Hall of Darkness
on the fifth level, right?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.240
By the way, are your summoning
techniques really okay?

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.950
I've never fought with a summoner before.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:11.790
True. There're so few of them, they're
practically an endangered species.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.880
It's basically more like a hobby now.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.380
What did you say?

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:24.260
What happened in the last 30 years?

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.310
But!

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:30.020
In that case, all the more reason
for me to correct your prejudices.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.270
I see, I'm looking forward to this.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.810
Then, if we're all ready, let's head in.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:38.280
Tact, make sure you don't get separated
from us. Mira, we're counting on you.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.610
I know, you don't need to tell me.

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:45.370
Ah, a light spirit blade.
An interesting item you have there.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.950
I'm surprised you knew what it was.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:51.210
Considering where we're going,
I borrowed this from the guild captain.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.790
She could tell that was
a light spirit blade?

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:55.840
Who is Mira?!

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.880
Anyway, that beautiful girl is the best!

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:06.180
Well, I think it's
about time I got it out.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:20.610
Cool!

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.610
This is an armor spirit...
what amazing power!

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:25.870
What fighting spirit!

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:29.490
Well? This is my summoned spirit.

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:32.290
He'll protect Tact completely.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.710
Wait, stop.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.540
It looks like something is there.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.670
This smell...

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:43.090
Nebrapolis' famous ghouls.

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:47.680
Hmm, what do you say we
test each other's strength?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.640
Going for first blood!

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.060
"Sorcery: Truest Crimson"

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:57.230
Leave the back to me!

00:12:58.730 --> 00:13:00.480
Mine!

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.950
Leftovers!

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:12.290
Ah, bravo! However... they sure do stink!

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.620
Or rather, as I recall,
deeper underground,

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:17.170
there are giant ghouls
and such as well.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.960
I'm calling it quits on questing properly.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.340
What?

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.060
Mira, what are you doing?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.100
Oh, just watch.

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:40.900
I put the question to the soaring maiden.

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:45.490
What is the name of one who banishes
evil with a flash of light for a sword?

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.280
Her name is Alfina.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:50.450
The name of a blade,
who swears allegiance to her master.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.580
Come to me!

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:11.600
Obeying your summons,
I have come, my master.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.890
It's been a long time, Alfina.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:17.560
Yes. But Master,

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.690
have you not changed a lot?

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:22.770
Well, a lot has happened.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:25.820
Hey, hey, Mira. Who is this?

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.150
This overflowing, amazing magical power...

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:30.570
Ah, Alfina of the Valkyries.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.330
My name is Alfina.
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.870
Wow.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.920
Master, your orders?

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.420
Yes, Valkyrie Alfina!

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:45.670
Annihilate all the monsters
below here to the fifth level!

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.630
As you wish!

00:15:19.790 --> 00:15:21.960
Annihilation completed.

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:22.830
Already?

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:26.710
Mm, thanks for your hard work. Go rest.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:37.390
Wow, it's amazing. There's really
no sign of any monsters.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.640
So these piles of ashes are
all the remains of monsters?

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:41.900
Seems like it.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:43.940
Oh, a Mobility Stone. Lucky me!

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:46.110
Woo-hoo! Yum, yum, yum!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:51.240
This is a C-Rank dungeon and for it
to turn into this casual stroll...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.820
Nothing wrong with that, right?

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:56.910
It's good that we can finish
quickly and go home early.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.420
This is the Mirror of Darkness?

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:10.050
To use it, just focus your thoughts
on who you want to see

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:11.930
and call out their names.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:12.880
Go on, Tact.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.760
O-Okay.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:21.430
My dad, Ashley. My mom, Leene.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.270
H-Huh?

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.520
Do you see anything?

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.610
No...

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:34.450
My dad... my mom...
they don't want to see me.

00:16:34.450 --> 00:16:37.280
Considering it's been left
on its own for so long,

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:39.910
I suppose there's also
a chance it no longer works.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:43.000
No way... After we came all this way...

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:46.170
Lyrica.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.720
Zef?

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.440
No way... Lyrica...

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:06.270
Delicious!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:09.190
Is that closer to what
our mom used to make?

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:14.820
Yeah, your cooking is getting better
and better. But are you doing okay?

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:18.200
Yeah, and I can't just
keep sleeping while you...

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.250
I'm... o... kay. Zef...

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.420
...good luck with your job...

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:46.440
Hey, what's a kid like you doing
on such a dangerous job?

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:50.150
This pays the best. My kid sister is sick,

00:17:50.150 --> 00:17:53.820
and we have no parents, so I have
to earn money for medicine.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:55.490
Sick...

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.240
Her symptoms are that
of the late stages

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.240
of the illness going around...

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:02.450
I hope we make it in time, but...

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:04.200
I'm finally home!

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:07.750
The lights are...

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:10.670
Lyrica! Lyrica!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.800
Lyrica... I...

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:17.180
I'm sorry... I'm sorry
I couldn't save you.

00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:18.510
Zef.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:21.930
If I had come home earlier... I...

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:24.140
It's not your fault, Zef.

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.060
I was sick, so it couldn't
be helped, right?

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:31.650
Besides... I don't want
to hear you say you're sorry.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:35.110
You worked so hard to be there for me,

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.990
and I wanted to say, "Thank you!"

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.120
O-Okay!

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.240
That's the Zef I know.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.660
Lyrica...

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:49.710
Man, all you've done is grown bigger.

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.960
You're still the same old crybaby.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.420
Asval...

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:55.130
You got this rare chance to see her.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:59.800
Is this down-in-the-dumps big brother
what you want to show her?

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.890
You're right... You've really
hit it on the nail.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:04.970
Listen to me, Lyrica.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:08.850
Since then, I've made friends
with members of this great guild.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:11.350
Nowadays, I can handle reconnaissance
and investigations,

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:14.320
and I take down enemies left
and right with my prized knife.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:16.690
I've become a great scout.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:23.280
So, you've become a wonderful adult,
and still stayed the big brother I love.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:28.000
Yeah, I'll keep on being the big brother
that you can be proud of.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.580
Yes, thank you.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:37.840
I'm glad... I got to see you.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:41.300
Later, my beloved big brother.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.850
I love you too, Lyrica.

00:19:57.610 --> 00:19:59.650
Sweat from my eyes...

00:19:59.650 --> 00:20:03.620
I'm... a big softie when
it comes to these things.

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.950
I've thought of them as NPCs,

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:09.450
but I see now that they each
have their own lives...

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.960
This is not confirmed, but...

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:15.040
...perhaps Tact's parents are still alive?

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:20.630
The Mirror of Darkness reflects
the dead, not the living.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.010
See?

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:24.680
But the people at
the Adventurers' Union said...

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.850
Oh, right!

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.970
If they were certified as dead

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:30.310
because it'd been five years
since they went missing...

00:20:30.310 --> 00:20:36.060
Yes, it would mean they do not have
direct confirmation of their deaths.

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.440
If they're alive,
you can definitely see them.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.190
So you keep a smile on your face!

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:43.320
That'll make your mom
and dad happier, right?

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:46.370
Yes, thank you very much!

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:50.620
Now, then, I suppose I'll give
that guy's request a try.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.000
Request?

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:57.710
...there's a little something I'd like
you to check while you're there.

00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:03.680
Remember how there used to be
an NPC demonologist

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:06.050
who chased after Lesser Demons
carrying tons of holy water?

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:08.760
I was thinking he might know
something about that incident

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.350
the other day with the Lesser Demon.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:16.520
Oh, Howard? I remember him.
But isn't he already dead?

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:17.900
That's right.

00:21:17.900 --> 00:21:20.570
Therefore, use the Mirror of Darkness.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:22.240
To reflect the dead,

00:21:22.240 --> 00:21:24.990
you need to be someone who had
a strong connection with them in life,

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:28.280
or have some deeply meaningful
memento. Or so they say.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:30.580
Will this really work?

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:33.660
Solomon said it wouldn't
hurt to try, but...

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:38.210
Hey, Howard. This is
the holy water that you loved.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:39.590
Come on out!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:43.130
Hmm? More?
You want more holy water?

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:45.760
You're not satisfied
just with what I have?

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:47.930
Umm... Mira?

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:49.930
What have you been trying to do?

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:53.350
Well, there was a guy I wanted
to call up for a bit, too,

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:55.350
but it seems that we don't share
a strong enough bond...

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.940
Mira's holy water...

00:21:57.940 --> 00:21:59.900
Mira, holy water...

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:04.690
Mira and... Mira and...
Mira and holy water!

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:09.240
It looks like I've awakened
some other scary thing!
